 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This is my poor heart's life, o'er sixty years,\nThe love I had for thee; it has disappeared\nAs the spring in summer disappears.\nIt was mine to keep the dead forever\nFrom that which dies: my death and his, alone,\nAnd mine between these two eyes were unknown,\nAnd his was mine beyond them. Alone\nI have seen all good things, he was only\nTo give them more beauty than myself.\nNo other vision of yourself\nMight not have changed me from myself,\nBut a woman's spirit from yourself.",
